# FieldKeel — Project Rules

Independent commercial multi-tenant SaaS. **Not** the MKMABALE/client app. Do not copy, import, or imitate prior client code, IA, or visuals.

Read `docs/product-requirements.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/database-design.md`, `docs/security-model.md`, `docs/design-system.md`, `docs/development-roadmap.md`.

Next.js 16 differs from older App Router docs. Before web code, check `web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. Prisma stays **v7** until the user explicitly approves an upgrade.

---

## Architecture

- Two apps: `web/` (Next.js App Router) and `api/` (NestJS ESM monolith). PostgreSQL is source of truth. MinIO/S3 holds bytes. Mail via SMTP.
- API owns permissions and workflow. Next.js is a client. No Prisma in `web/`. No business API as Next route handlers.
- No Redis, RabbitMQ, Kubernetes, or extra microservices unless explicitly requested.
- Critical writes use Prisma transactions and write `AuditEvent` in the same transaction when practical.
- Timestamps stored UTC. Organization IANA timezone is used for “today”, timesheets, and overtime.
- Soft-deactivate referenced entities. Do not cascade-delete operational history.
- Do not store business records in `localStorage` / `sessionStorage`. UI chrome flags only (sidebar collapsed, theme).

```ts
// BAD — second source of truth
localStorage.setItem("jobs", JSON.stringify(jobs));

// GOOD — UI preference only
localStorage.setItem("fieldops.rail-collapsed", "1");
```

---

## Multi-tenancy

- A User may belong to many organizations. Platform role on `User`: `USER` | `SUPER_ADMIN`. Org role **only** on `OrganizationMembership`: `OWNER` | `ADMIN` | `OPERATIONS_MANAGER` | `SUPERVISOR` | `TECHNICIAN`.
- Never add `User.role` for org permissions. Never put `organizationId` on `User`.
- Frontend org id/slug is **selection**, not authorization. Load ACTIVE membership server-side on every tenant request. Bind `RequestContext` from that membership.
- Ignore or reject body `organizationId` on tenant resource routes if it disagrees with context.
- Tenant rows always persist `organizationId`. Look up by `{ id, organizationId }`, never id alone. Wrong-tenant IDs → **404**. In-org forbidden actions → **403**.
- SUPER_ADMIN does not silently read tenant jobs/files. Platform routes are separate.

```ts
// BAD
prisma.job.findUnique({ where: { id: jobId } });

// GOOD
prisma.job.findFirst({ where: { id: jobId, organizationId: ctx.organizationId } });
```

