## Security

- Session: HTTP-only cookies (`fieldops_access`, `fieldops_refresh`). **Never** put JWTs in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or SPA JSON for storage.
- Do not embed `orgRole` / `organizationId` in access JWTs as authority; read membership from DB.
- Store hashes of refresh and invitation tokens, not plaintext.
- CORS allow-list `WEB_URL` with credentials. No `origin: *`.
- Never return `passwordHash`, token hashes, or raw tokens in DTOs.
- Uploads: auth + org scope, size cap, MIME allow-list, magic-byte check, private bucket, keys `org/{organizationId}/...`. Authorize downloads via parent record.
- Presigned GET URLs are short-lived capability tokens issued only after tenant/job authorization (`S3_PRESIGNED_GET_EXPIRY_SECONDS`, default 300). Never persist them; never log signed URLs; never issue PUT/DELETE presigns from generic download endpoints.
- **Rich text / XSS (future):** Do not render user-controlled HTML or Markdown as raw HTML. If a future feature needs rich text, sanitize with an approved sanitizer library and never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` (or equivalent) on unsanitized tenant content. Plain JSON text fields are not an XSS sink.
- `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true, transform: true })`.
- Rate-limit auth. Helmet in bootstrap.

```ts
// BAD
localStorage.setItem("accessToken", token);

// GOOD
// Set-Cookie HttpOnly from Nest; browser fetch credentials: "include"
```

