## Naming

- Product: **FieldKeel**. Packages stay `web` and `api`.
- DB/Prisma models: PascalCase singular (`OrganizationMembership`, `ClockEvent`).
- Tables: Prisma default. Columns: camelCase in Prisma.
- Files: kebab-case. Nest: `jobs.module.ts`, `create-job.dto.ts`.
- React components: PascalCase. Org customers are `Client` (not FieldKeel tenants).
- Cookies: `fieldops_*` (legacy technical cookie names — do not rename). Env: `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_*`, `S3_*`, `SMTP_*`. Public web: only `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`.

---

## API conventions

- Prefix `/api`, version `/v1` → `/api/v1/...`.
- Nest ESM: import with `.js` extensions as in existing files.
- REST, DTO classes + class-validator. Controllers thin; services hold rules (job transitions, last owner, completion evidence).
- Auth from cookies (Passport extractor), not required `Authorization` header for the browser app.
- List endpoints: org filter + role scope (technician = assigned only). Paginate. Sort allow-list.
- Errors: consistent JSON `{ statusCode, message, error }`. No stack traces in production.

```ts
// BAD — technician posts arbitrary completion
@Patch(":id")
update(@Body() dto: { status: string }) { return this.jobs.save(dto); }

// GOOD — explicit command
@Post(":id/complete")
complete(@Req() req: AuthedRequest) { return this.jobs.complete(req.ctx); }
```

